# Zombies Aren't Real - English language file (the localization source).
#
# Format: one `key = value` per line; `#` / `;` start a comment. A value may contain
# named placeholders written as {name}; the game replaces each {name} with a runtime
# value (see Lf in src/lang.odin). Escapes in a value: \n = newline, \t = tab, \\ = a
# literal backslash. Leading/trailing spaces around the key and value are trimmed, so a
# string that must start or end with a space needs no special handling here (none do).
#
# To add a new language: copy this file to lang/<code>.lang (e.g. lang/fr.lang), set
# language.name/language.code below, and translate every value. Keep the KEYS and the
# {placeholder} names identical - only the English text between them is translated. The
# game lists every lang/*.lang on the settings screen under "Language / Localization".
#
# Keys are namespaced by screen: menu.* (startup menu), pause.* (Esc menu), settings.*,
# credits.*, confirm.* (yes/no dialogs), loadout.*, toolbar.* / bar.* (command bar), hud.* (in-game
# text), endscreen.* (end-of-level popup), tutorial.*, bugreport.*, replay.*, badge.*.

# - language metadata (shown in the settings selector) -
