editor.about.box = Drag from corner to corner. Most buildings are rectangles: draw them fast, then rotate them with Q / E.
editor.about.building = Click each corner. Click the first corner again (or press Enter) to finish.
editor.about.slice = Draw a straight cut line right across a building: it comes apart into separate buildings along the line, each keeping the height, use and type. A line that ends inside a building leaves it whole.
editor.about.move = Drag a building (or anything else) to move it whole. No corner handles get in the way, so even a small building far out is easy to grab. Shift+click adds to what moves; drag empty ground to select an area.
