editor.dlg.help_title = MAP EDITOR HELP
editor.help_scroll = WHEEL OR UP / DOWN SCROLLS
editor.help.1 = TOOLS (keys 1-9, 0, K, M)
editor.help.2 = 1 SELECT edits what is drawn, M MOVE drags whole buildings about (no corner handles in the way). 2 STANDARD BUILDING drags out a rectangular building, 3 CUSTOM BUILDING clicks out any shape, 4 ROAD and 5 BRIDGE click out lines, 6 WATER draws water, islands, rivers and coastlines, 7 PARK parks and woods, 8 NO-CIV keeps civilians out of a circle, 9 STAGES draws each stage's play area, K SLICE cuts buildings apart along a line, 0 REFERENCE IMAGE puts a picture from your computer under the map to trace over (I hides it).
editor.help.3 = DRAWING
editor.help.4 = A tool stays armed after it draws. Click to place points; Enter, a double-click or clicking the first corner finishes. Right-click or Backspace takes back a point; Esc drops the shape, then the tool.
editor.help.5 = SNAPPING
editor.help.6 = Points snap to the grid (SNAP or G sets 1 / 2 / 5 / 10 m, or off) and onto any corner near the cursor (a green ring). Hold Alt to place a point exactly.
editor.help.7 = SELECTING AND EDITING
editor.help.8 = Click selects, Shift+click (or Ctrl+click) adds or removes, a drag on empty ground selects an area (Shift+drag adds to it, Ctrl+drag takes it out), Ctrl+A everything, Ctrl+Shift+A everything like what is selected (every bridge, every police station), Ctrl+I everything else. A mix of things selected can be narrowed with KEEP ONLY. Drag a selection to move it; arrows nudge it (Shift: x10). Q / E rotate it 15 degrees (Shift: 1); L flips it left to right (Shift+L: top to bottom). Drag a corner to reshape; drag a dot on an edge to add a corner; right-click a corner (or press Del / X with the cursor on it) to delete it. K SLICE draws a cut line across buildings: each one it runs right through comes apart into separate buildings.
editor.help.9 = COPY, DELETE, UNDO
editor.help.10 = Ctrl+D duplicates beside, Ctrl+C / Ctrl+X / Ctrl+V copy, cut and paste at the cursor (into another map too), Del or X deletes. Ctrl+Z undoes, Ctrl+Y (or Ctrl+Shift+Z) redoes.
editor.help.11 = BUILDINGS
editor.help.12 = Each building has a height (snipers and mortars on a taller roof reach farther), a use, and a TYPE: a police station arms a garrison, a hospital pays in a safe zone, a gas station explodes, a school makes walls tougher. HEIGHTS and TYPES (H / T) colour the map by them.
editor.help.13 = STAGES
editor.help.14 = A map plays as levels, one per stage. Each stage is a play area that must contain the one before; with no play area the whole map plays. The outbreak and the budget come from the stage's land unless a STAGE SETTING says otherwise.
editor.help.15 = CHECKING AND PLAYING
editor.help.16 = CHECK (and every save) shows in red what nobody can reach - an island with no bridge, a walled-in yard - and lists each bridge nobody can cross under WARNINGS in the map panel: click one to go to it, DISMISS to hide it for good. TEST PLAY saves and plays the map; the pause menu's BACK TO EDITOR comes back here.
editor.help.17 = THE VIEW
editor.help.18 = Wheel zooms, hold {key:pan_drag} and drag to pan (the game's Pan drag control), W A S D pan, F fits the whole map.
editor.help.19 = SHARING
editor.help.20 = PUBLISH uploads the map to the Steam Workshop for everyone; publishing again updates it. Maps you subscribe to appear in the main menu.
editor.help.21 = STAGE SETTINGS A MAP CAN CHANGE (+ OTHER SETTING)
editor.help.22 = Outbreak: outbreak.spawns, spawns_at_1km2, zombies_per_spawn, spawn_radius, spawn_radius_at_1km2; zombie.speed; battle.cleanup_quiet_seconds, cleanup_seconds. Crowd: civilian.people_per_building_area. Budget: economy.unspent_bonus_percent. Badges: badges.bronze / silver / gold / diamond / sapphire / emerald / ruby_percent. Prices: the cost of sniper, mortar, turret, mine, c4 and battleship (sniper.cost ...), garrison.cost_base / cost_per_meter / cost_max, evac.corridor_start_fee, evac.corridor_area_cost, evac.hold_cost. Walls: walls.cost, hp. Special buildings: building_class.money. Loadout: <item>.sp_cost and <item>.max (airstrike, paratroopers, helicopter, gas_bomb, fire_bomb, call_to_arms, apc, bus, medevac, bulldozer, tank).
editor.help.23 = EXPANDING A MAP
editor.help.24 = A map made from a postal code can grow: EXPAND MAP shows the map's squares, and a click on a + square brings in that piece of the city - its buildings, roads, water and parks - from the game's map server. Squares already queued keep arriving after you put the grid away; Ctrl+Z takes the last one back out. A map you drew yourself has no real place to grow into.
